would have been too tall with the carrier.

00:20:36.040 --> 00:20:37.701
- Okay, well that's good for both of us.

00:20:37.701 --> 00:20:38.870
- I would have just taken your carrier

00:20:38.870 --> 00:20:40.380
and I would have just set
it in the snow somewhere.

00:20:40.380 --> 00:20:41.277
It would have gotten
four feet on top of it

00:20:41.277 --> 00:20:44.220
and it would still be
in Mammoth under snow.

00:20:44.220 --> 00:20:46.570
So, you're welcome for
not taking your carrier.

00:20:48.810 --> 00:20:53.810
I get up to Mammoth and I
started to see that lots of snow,

00:20:53.960 --> 00:20:56.863
like it went from no
snow, like, I don't know--

00:20:56.863 --> 00:20:58.657
- I can't imagine 11 feet of snow.

00:20:58.657 --> 00:21:00.630
- If you ever driven up,
you never driven up there?

00:21:00.630 --> 00:21:01.650
- No, never been up there.

00:21:01.650 --> 00:21:04.660
- So, you drive through this
thing called the Owens Valley

00:21:04.660 --> 00:21:07.070
which is there's all this
history of the Owens Valley

00:21:07.070 --> 00:21:10.070
and how there was this giant lake up there

00:21:10.070 --> 00:21:13.960
and then Mulholland who
Mulholland Drive is named after

00:21:13.960 --> 00:21:16.072
and lots of things in LA are named after.

00:21:16.072 --> 00:21:16.930
Like I've--

00:21:16.930 --> 00:21:20.210
- Owen Wilson's hanging out
up there, Terrell Owens.

00:21:20.210 --> 00:21:24.600
- This guy owned or worked for the LADWP,

00:21:24.600 --> 00:21:25.650
Department of Water and Power

00:21:25.650 --> 00:21:28.010
and then he bought a bunch of land,

00:21:28.010 --> 00:21:30.520
all the privately available
land in this valley

00:21:30.520 --> 00:21:32.430
and that gave him the water rights

00:21:32.430 --> 00:21:35.170
to this giant lake that
they basically drained

00:21:35.170 --> 00:21:37.480
and this is where LA got
a bunch of its water from

00:21:37.480 --> 00:21:40.060
and now, all this water
that comes into this valley

00:21:40.060 --> 00:21:42.020
is pumped to Los Angeles.

00:21:42.020 --> 00:21:44.000
It's quite interesting
if you're interested

00:21:44.000 --> 00:21:46.260
in the history of the
water of Los Angeles.

00:21:46.260 --> 00:21:47.380
- That's another podcast, so.

00:21:47.380 --> 00:21:49.110
- But anyway, the trip up there

00:21:49.110 --> 00:21:51.610
is just this desolate nothingness

00:21:51.610 --> 00:21:53.780
with a couple of towns that you come to,

00:21:53.780 --> 00:21:56.620
like it could be a town
and it'll be like 50 miles

00:21:56.620 --> 00:22:00.340
and nothing except just these
mountain ranges on each side.

00:22:00.340 --> 00:22:01.173
We went through--

00:22:01.173 --> 00:22:02.006
- But beautiful.

00:22:02.006 --> 00:22:03.230
- Beautiful, absolutely beautiful.

00:22:03.230 --> 00:22:05.050
You know Lone Pine.

00:22:05.050 --> 00:22:06.650
You probably heard of this town.

00:22:07.930 --> 00:22:10.750
There's been like a hundred
movie shot in Lone Pine

00:22:10.750 --> 00:22:12.450
including Django Unchained

00:22:12.450 --> 00:22:14.240
and a bunch of other ones
that you've heard of.

00:22:14.240 --> 00:22:15.570
- Uh-huh.
- And the mountains

00:22:15.570 --> 00:22:17.680
right outside of Lone Pine looked,

00:22:17.680 --> 00:22:18.619
I kind of looked at,

00:22:18.619 --> 00:22:21.290
I was like that looks like the Himalayas

00:22:21.290 --> 00:22:22.300
like the way that,

00:22:22.300 --> 00:22:25.510
it was these rocky mountains,
just straight rocks

00:22:25.510 --> 00:22:27.930
with snow on them

00:22:27.930 --> 00:22:29.550
and then I started reading
about it on my phone

00:22:29.550 --> 00:22:31.415
once I was up at Mammoth, they were like,

00:22:31.415 --> 00:22:34.740
often filmmakers used the
mountains outside of Lone Pine

00:22:34.740 --> 00:22:36.970
to pass for the Himalayas
in low-budget movies.

00:22:36.970 --> 00:22:38.430
I was like, ha!

00:22:38.430 --> 00:22:39.860
- Didn't you feel validated?
- Yahoo!

00:22:39.860 --> 00:22:40.693
That's right, buddy.

00:22:40.693 --> 00:22:42.700
- You felt low-budget validated.

00:22:42.700 --> 00:22:45.150
- Anyway, we get very close to Mammoth

00:22:45.150 --> 00:22:47.547
and I see the sign, chains required

00:22:47.547 --> 00:22:49.600
and my heart rate goes up a little bit.

00:22:49.600 --> 00:22:50.660
- Yeah, yeah.

00:22:50.660 --> 00:22:52.110
- I'm like this is the moment of truth.

00:22:52.110 --> 00:22:54.250
I've got to pull off to
the side of the road.

00:22:54.250 --> 00:22:56.576
Keep in mind that not
only are they getting snow

00:22:56.576 --> 00:23:01.010
but it's seven degrees.

00:23:01.010 --> 00:23:02.340
- Ooh.

00:23:02.340 --> 00:23:05.670
Was it snowing at Des Moines at that time?

00:23:05.670 --> 00:23:08.340
- It was just a teeny
bit of snow was starting.

00:23:08.340 --> 00:23:09.560
- Was there's snow on the street?

00:23:09.560 --> 00:23:11.312
- No snow on the ground.

00:23:11.312 --> 00:23:14.221
First of all, I wasn't all
the way to Mammoth and so,

00:23:14.221 --> 00:23:18.100
the machines they have that
get the snow off of the road,

00:23:18.100 --> 00:23:21.320
it's absolutely amazing
how efficient they are

00:23:21.320 --> 00:23:24.900
at getting mounds and mounds
of snow off of the road

00:23:24.900 --> 00:23:27.170
and then of course because
they sawed the road,

00:23:27.170 --> 00:23:29.080
there was nothing on the
road, it was completely dry

00:23:29.080 --> 00:23:31.350
but it was like preemptively
putting on chains.

00:23:31.350 --> 00:23:32.183
- Okay.

00:23:32.183 --> 00:23:34.020
- Some people weren't
stopping, some people,

00:23:34.920 --> 00:23:36.920
I found out later why some
people were continuing to go

00:23:36.920 --> 00:23:41.920
but I pull over, I was so
prepared, I had a headlamp.

00:23:42.000 --> 00:23:43.010
- Was it night?

00:23:43.010 --> 00:23:43.940
- It was already dark.
- Or you just

00:23:43.940 --> 00:23:45.670
wanted to wear a headlamp
because you had it.

00:23:45.670 --> 00:23:48.410
- I had a headlamp, I
had another little light

00:23:48.410 --> 00:23:52.100
that I put under the car,
I had a tarp or a tarpaulin

00:23:52.100 --> 00:23:53.620
is the full name for that.

00:23:53.620 --> 00:23:54.860
- You got tarpaulin.

00:23:54.860 --> 00:23:57.680
- Yeah, so you'd get down on the ground.

00:23:57.680 --> 00:23:59.140
- You laid out a blanket for yourself?

00:23:59.140 --> 00:24:02.880
- I'd added so hard on the tarp.

00:24:02.880 --> 00:24:06.340
- Look, take a picture of
me laying out on a tarp.

00:24:06.340 --> 00:24:08.047
- And there's people going--

00:24:08.047 --> 00:24:09.100
- Get my headlamp.

00:24:09.100 --> 00:24:10.860
- Going past me, you know?

00:24:10.860 --> 00:24:13.930
And I'm out there on the
tarp and reaching around

00:24:13.930 --> 00:24:18.020
and clamping it down and
hoping that I'm not endangering

00:24:18.020 --> 00:24:20.573
the lives of my children and wife.

00:24:21.560 --> 00:24:23.520
- That guy doesn't use a Bro Dryer.

00:24:23.520 --> 00:24:25.127
- I eventually got it on there.

00:24:25.127 --> 00:24:29.530
- Sticks his head out
the window of his Harley.

00:24:29.530 --> 00:24:31.610
- And then I get back into the car

00:24:31.610 --> 00:24:34.080
and I start driving down the dry pavement

00:24:34.080 --> 00:24:36.143
with the chains on the tires.

00:24:36.143 --> 00:24:37.170
- That can't be good.

00:24:37.170 --> 00:24:40.300
- And then I'm like, where's the snow?

00:24:40.300 --> 00:24:41.713
Like, I don't feel right about this.

00:24:41.713 --> 00:24:43.920
I'm like, Jessie Google how fast,

00:24:43.920 --> 00:24:45.430
I was going like 40.

00:24:45.430 --> 00:24:47.820
I was like Google how fast you should go

00:24:47.820 --> 00:24:49.870
with chains on your tires on dry pavement.

00:24:49.870 --> 00:24:50.997
- What did it feel like?

00:24:50.997 --> 00:24:52.105
(imitating rattling)

00:24:52.105 --> 00:24:54.030
- It that was crazy but when
you get to a certain speed,

00:24:54.030 --> 00:24:55.400
it kind of just all blends together

00:24:55.400 --> 00:24:57.530
and it just kind of becomes this low hum.

00:24:57.530 --> 00:25:00.150
- I mean just literally, your rubber tires

00:25:00.150 --> 00:25:02.470
are wrapped in chains, that's crazy.

00:25:02.470 --> 00:25:05.477
- Anyway, 20 to 30.

00:25:05.477 --> 00:25:07.330
- 30 miles per hour?

00:25:07.330 --> 00:25:09.610
- And so I slowed it down.

00:25:09.610 --> 00:25:13.700
It took like 45 minutes to
go the last like 10 miles

00:25:14.780 --> 00:25:15.643
and eventually once we got to Mammoth,

00:25:15.643 --> 00:25:17.010
there's still no snow.

00:25:17.010 --> 00:25:18.590
Like very little snow on,

00:25:18.590 --> 00:25:20.140
there's a couple of
icy patches or whatever

00:25:20.140 --> 00:25:23.030
but chains were still required
but once you got into town,

00:25:23.030 --> 00:25:25.350
that was when they had taken,

00:25:25.350 --> 00:25:28.320
it was like driving through a corn maze

00:25:28.320 --> 00:25:29.713
but the corn was snow.

00:25:29.713 --> 00:25:30.677
- Wow.
- So like,

00:25:30.677 --> 00:25:34.910
you can't see anything
except these huge snowbanks.

00:25:34.910 --> 00:25:36.660
- Like shops?

00:25:36.660 --> 00:25:37.690
- Everywhere.

00:25:37.690 --> 00:25:40.530
Like, I don't know how they so quickly

00:25:40.530 --> 00:25:42.060
got access to everything.

00:25:42.060 --> 00:25:45.260
Like, every parking lot,
and every restaurant

00:25:45.260 --> 00:25:47.410
and every shop was completely cleared

00:25:47.410 --> 00:25:49.500
but they had just moved all the snow

00:25:49.500 --> 00:25:51.350
and snow obviously compacts a whole lot

00:25:51.350 --> 00:25:53.950
like if you've got 11 feet
of snow, 15 feet of snow,

00:25:54.830 --> 00:25:56.090
that's just falling fresh,

00:25:56.090 --> 00:25:58.230
you can squish all that down into,

00:25:58.230 --> 00:25:59.870
I don't know, a couple of feet.

00:25:59.870 --> 00:26:02.350
- But they probably had
salted it so the stuff melted.

00:26:02.350 --> 00:26:03.391
It wasn't like they had to push it.

00:26:03.391 --> 00:26:05.860
- The road was still
dry but you were driving

00:26:05.860 --> 00:26:08.143
through this corn maze of snow.

00:26:09.150 --> 00:26:10.650
- Did you take photos of this?

00:26:12.600 --> 00:26:13.433
- No.

00:26:13.433 --> 00:26:18.020
- Now, was anybody else
driving with chains?

00:26:18.020 --> 00:26:19.880
- Yeah, once I got into
town, everybody had them on.

00:26:19.880 --> 00:26:20.940
- Everybody?
- 'Cause it was--

00:26:20.940 --> 00:26:21.773
- You're validated.

00:26:21.773 --> 00:26:22.660
- It was required.

00:26:22.660 --> 00:26:24.210
- 'Cause you were thinking
maybe I should pull over

00:26:24.210 --> 00:26:27.410
and take them back off and
that would be admitting defeat.

00:26:27.410 --> 00:26:28.900
- Yeah, but it was just
one of those moments

00:26:28.900 --> 00:26:29.733
where I was just--

00:26:29.733 --> 00:26:30.770
- Dads don't do that.

00:26:30.770 --> 00:26:33.300
- I could have paid, in fact,
there were dudes out there.

00:26:33.300 --> 00:26:34.490
- Dad don't defeat.

00:26:34.490 --> 00:26:37.890
- Charging $40 for to put
the chains on for you.

00:26:37.890 --> 00:26:38.840
- Just to put them on?

00:26:38.840 --> 00:26:40.270
- They didn't have chains.

00:26:40.270 --> 00:26:42.000
They just had the service.

00:26:42.000 --> 00:26:43.280
- And tarpaulin 'em, probably.

00:26:43.280 --> 00:26:45.520
- Yeah, and they were
like dressed like firemen

00:26:46.540 --> 00:26:47.900
which I found interesting and ironic

00:26:47.900 --> 00:26:49.485
considering you're on a fire vacation.

00:26:49.485 --> 00:26:52.208
- Right, so we.

00:26:52.208 --> 00:26:54.390
All right, so we got you to
Mammoth, let's get me to Cabo.

00:26:54.390 --> 00:26:58.940
Now, I went to a place that
I've been three years earlier.

00:26:58.940 --> 00:27:00.693
Christy and I went to this place.

00:27:01.960 --> 00:27:03.820
I'll give a shout out to The Cape.

00:27:03.820 --> 00:27:05.090
I really enjoy it.

00:27:05.090 --> 00:27:07.010
It's a nice spot.

00:27:07.010 --> 00:27:07.843
- I've been there once.

00:27:07.843 --> 00:27:09.910
- Not a sponsor, I recommended
it to you and you went.

00:27:09.910 --> 00:27:13.113
And then I decided I was
gonna go back and I did.

00:27:15.200 --> 00:27:17.890
Of course, when you went
back a few months back,

00:27:17.890 --> 00:27:20.490
you didn't go back to the same place.

00:27:20.490 --> 00:27:22.320
You went to a different place.

00:27:22.320 --> 00:27:23.153
- Nothing against The Cape.

00:27:23.153 --> 00:27:25.550
- Northing against The Cape but for me,

00:27:25.550 --> 00:27:26.810
it's like I knew what I was gonna get

00:27:26.810 --> 00:27:28.280
and I wanted more of it.

00:27:28.280 --> 00:27:30.110
- I'm always up for a new thing.

00:27:30.110 --> 00:27:32.370
I just wanted to try something.

00:27:32.370 --> 00:27:35.310
- Yeah, sometimes I want the same thing.

00:27:35.310 --> 00:27:36.870
- And if I hadn't had tried something new,

00:27:36.870 --> 00:27:37.930
I wouldn't have gotten Gary

00:27:37.930 --> 00:27:40.160
to take that frickin' picture
of me in my watermelon outfit.

00:27:40.160 --> 00:27:41.910
- Which brought me back to Instagram.

00:27:41.910 --> 00:27:42.937
- Yeah, so again.

00:27:42.937 --> 00:27:44.730
- I'm not faulting you.
- You should be happy.

00:27:44.730 --> 00:27:46.250
- There's a little
different psychology here

00:27:46.250 --> 00:27:47.300
between the two of us.

00:27:47.300 --> 00:27:48.640
First of all, it was a shorter,

00:27:48.640 --> 00:27:52.480
it was just a short,
well, a longer weekend

00:27:52.480 --> 00:27:54.380
so a shorter vacation,
wasn't like a whole week

00:27:54.380 --> 00:27:59.380
so I just wanted to have
this relaxing poolside place,

00:28:01.380 --> 00:28:03.753
place that I was gonna go
to and I could count on it

00:28:03.753 --> 00:28:07.390
because I only had a couple of
days to make the most of it.

00:28:07.390 --> 00:28:08.580
It started out much better

00:28:08.580 --> 00:28:11.650
'cause the previous time that we went,

00:28:11.650 --> 00:28:16.380
we were flying down there and
we were getting on the plane

00:28:16.380 --> 00:28:18.710
and the first class was already on

00:28:18.710 --> 00:28:21.700
and we had some friends,
I'll call him acquaintances,

00:28:21.700 --> 00:28:24.327
well, let's call him
friends, people who knew us.

00:28:24.327 --> 00:28:27.040
You know, like hey,
recognize us and we went back

00:28:27.040 --> 00:28:28.680
and once we got in the air,

00:28:28.680 --> 00:28:31.513
they sent back some champagne to us.

00:28:32.349 --> 00:28:35.630
The flight attendant came up and said

00:28:35.630 --> 00:28:37.480
this is from your friends in first class

00:28:37.480 --> 00:28:40.930
and they gave us champagne
or mimosas or something.

00:28:40.930 --> 00:28:42.100
- Who friends?

00:28:42.100 --> 00:28:42.933
- It was,

00:28:45.870 --> 00:28:48.680
Ran and you know it was them.

00:28:48.680 --> 00:28:50.040
- Oh.

00:28:50.040 --> 00:28:53.670
- So, anyway, we drink the champagne

00:28:54.730 --> 00:28:59.455
and I think there was
this weird interaction.

00:28:59.455 --> 00:29:02.970
I don't know for sure
but I think that Christy

00:29:02.970 --> 00:29:04.780
had taken an anxiety medication

00:29:04.780 --> 00:29:07.230
because she has problems with flying.

00:29:07.230 --> 00:29:08.590
- Yes.

00:29:08.590 --> 00:29:11.290
- And then by the time
we got off the plane,

00:29:11.290 --> 00:29:15.300
she's not feeling great and
then we had to take this taxi,

00:29:15.300 --> 00:29:17.080
it's like a 25-minute drive

00:29:18.010 --> 00:29:20.713
so we're like taking a
taxi to the place and like,

00:29:21.742 --> 00:29:24.540
she's not looking like she feels great.

00:29:24.540 --> 00:29:27.511
- This vacation's not
starting great, fire vacation.

00:29:27.511 --> 00:29:29.410
Fire alarm.

00:29:29.410 --> 00:29:32.150
- And literally, when we
pulled up to the place

00:29:32.150 --> 00:29:34.150
and they like open the door
and they're like hello,

00:29:34.150 --> 00:29:35.048
welcome to the resort,

00:29:35.048 --> 00:29:38.770
like grand entrance type welcome situation

00:29:38.770 --> 00:29:40.410
and it's a beautiful place

00:29:40.410 --> 00:29:43.110
like right when you walk up to check-in,

00:29:43.110 --> 00:29:47.920
you're like looking out over
the beach and it's amazing

00:29:47.920 --> 00:29:49.600
and as I'm walking up,

00:29:49.600 --> 00:29:53.300
Christy's like I've got to find a bathroom

00:29:53.300 --> 00:29:57.040
and like she bolts past me

00:29:57.040 --> 00:29:59.430
and like I'm taking in this wonderful view

00:29:59.430 --> 00:30:01.920
and I just had this image of Christy

00:30:01.920 --> 00:30:06.210
like sprinting past me, sprinting
past the reception area,

00:30:06.210 --> 00:30:08.070
turns out she asked them
where's the nearest restroom

00:30:08.070 --> 00:30:09.500
but I feel so far ahead of me,

00:30:09.500 --> 00:30:11.360
it just looked like she didn't even stop.

00:30:11.360 --> 00:30:13.133
She just disappears.

00:30:16.550 --> 00:30:18.550
She eventually comes out
until she'd found a bathroom,

00:30:18.550 --> 00:30:20.730
she was like throwing up
in the bathroom and stuff

00:30:20.730 --> 00:30:22.290
and then she had to go up to the,

00:30:22.290 --> 00:30:23.250
right, we checked into the room,

00:30:23.250 --> 00:30:25.470
she had to like lay down for two hours.

00:30:25.470 --> 00:30:27.140
It's a horrible beginning
of that vacation.

00:30:27.140 --> 00:30:30.010
After that, everything
got a lot better for her.

00:30:30.010 --> 00:30:31.696
- Well, that's one way to see it.

00:30:31.696 --> 00:30:34.913
You start that low, you're
gonna have a good time.

00:30:36.670 --> 00:30:38.170
- Maybe I threw her under the bus

00:30:38.170 --> 00:30:40.170
with this whole medication champagne thing

00:30:40.170 --> 00:30:43.360
but that's what happened and then so,

00:30:43.360 --> 00:30:45.823
this time, we didn't make
any of those mistakes.

00:30:47.070 --> 00:30:48.640
We get there and everything was good

00:30:48.640 --> 00:30:50.943
so we got there all in one piece.

00:30:52.639 --> 00:30:54.840
I mean the theme of my vacation

00:30:54.840 --> 00:30:58.930
was I don't wanna see no
mountains, I wanna see no snow,

00:30:58.930 --> 00:31:01.100
I don't wanna do anything
active like skiing.

00:31:01.100 --> 00:31:03.470
I wanted to do the opposite of you.

00:31:03.470 --> 00:31:07.440
I wanted to lay flat on the sand,

00:31:07.440 --> 00:31:08.747
take one picture for Instagram

00:31:08.747 --> 00:31:11.403
and I wanna lay flat on a lounger,

00:31:13.060 --> 00:31:18.060
drink some drinks, read some
books, be with my lovely wife.

00:31:21.793 --> 00:31:25.310
And that's it and mission
accomplished, man.

00:31:25.310 --> 00:31:26.900
It was great.

00:31:26.900 --> 00:31:28.360
Especially because it didn't start off

00:31:28.360 --> 00:31:30.990
with her sprinting past me.

00:31:30.990 --> 00:31:33.140
There was no sprinting to any restrooms.

00:31:33.140 --> 00:31:35.920
So, that's now my like
