there grabbing the chicken leg

00:40:35.170 --> 00:40:36.240
and before you know it,

00:40:36.240 --> 00:40:39.470
you're like ham-fisted grabbing your thigh

00:40:39.470 --> 00:40:42.330
with one hand and the chicken
leg with the other hand

00:40:42.330 --> 00:40:44.300
and you're just wrenching them apart

00:40:44.300 --> 00:40:47.320
to try to pull apart and
have a leg experience

00:40:47.320 --> 00:40:49.650
separate from a thigh experience.

00:40:49.650 --> 00:40:50.940
- Gotta be careful with that though.

00:40:50.940 --> 00:40:52.277
- And you're just (imitating creaking).

00:40:53.859 --> 00:40:54.740
Just trying to get the part--
- Just pull the bone

00:40:54.740 --> 00:40:55.573
all the way out.

00:40:55.573 --> 00:40:59.450
- Right, you'll get the thigh
bone out of all the thigh meat

00:40:59.450 --> 00:41:01.940
stuck to the end of the drumstick.

00:41:01.940 --> 00:41:03.070
- Oh, I was thinking the opposite.

00:41:03.070 --> 00:41:04.930
Sometimes, you pull the
drumstick right out of the thigh.

00:41:04.930 --> 00:41:08.033
- Either way, it's not good
when the analogy is to my body.

00:41:09.370 --> 00:41:11.710
I felt sure that was gonna happen.

00:41:11.710 --> 00:41:12.910
- I doubt that she could pull it out.

00:41:12.910 --> 00:41:14.307
- I mean it was like,

00:41:14.307 --> 00:41:17.270
I was just having imagery
of that Mortal Kombat

00:41:17.270 --> 00:41:19.360
finishing move where like
it got pulls the head

00:41:19.360 --> 00:41:20.580
and the spine out of the body.

00:41:20.580 --> 00:41:23.850
It's like, she's gonna pull my leg.

00:41:23.850 --> 00:41:27.150
- Did you make any grunts or
did you make any signals that--

00:41:27.150 --> 00:41:29.150
- I was breathing so heavily--
- She's going too far.

00:41:29.150 --> 00:41:31.230
- That Christy told me afterward

00:41:31.230 --> 00:41:34.420
that she almost asked me to be quiet.

00:41:34.420 --> 00:41:35.725
Like she didn't ask me

00:41:35.725 --> 00:41:36.720
are you okay?
- You were ruining

00:41:36.720 --> 00:41:37.710
her massage.

00:41:37.710 --> 00:41:39.039
- She wasn't gonna ask, are you okay?

00:41:39.039 --> 00:41:39.872
(Rhett grunting)

00:41:39.872 --> 00:41:41.693
She was gonna ask, can you be quiet?

00:41:42.720 --> 00:41:44.700
She's like, why are you breathing so loud?

00:41:44.700 --> 00:41:47.543
I looked over, I was just like,
did you see me in my diaper?

00:41:49.042 --> 00:41:49.875
- 'Cause you were in pain.

00:41:49.875 --> 00:41:53.050
- I love the pain but I got
a go to physical therapy

00:41:53.050 --> 00:41:53.883
for this thing.

00:41:53.883 --> 00:41:54.716
- Still hurts?

00:41:54.716 --> 00:41:55.549
- Yes, still hurts.

00:41:56.776 --> 00:41:58.280
That's my near-death experience.

00:41:58.280 --> 00:41:59.540
Top that.

00:41:59.540 --> 00:42:03.440
- Okay, so, because it
was snowing so much--

00:42:03.440 --> 00:42:05.370
- Next time you eat a
chicken leg, think of me.

00:42:05.370 --> 00:42:07.570
- And because it was so windy,

00:42:07.570 --> 00:42:11.770
the top of the mountain was
closed for a couple of reason.

00:42:11.770 --> 00:42:16.770
Like, they're worried about
visibility and avalanches

00:42:17.350 --> 00:42:18.620
and wind gusts, like the wind gusts

00:42:18.620 --> 00:42:20.950
at the top of the mountain
were over 50 miles per hour

00:42:20.950 --> 00:42:25.000
and so they're very like
hesitant to open up the mountain

