01:04:17.800 --> 01:04:20.330
that then we left your house
so we couldn't finish watching.

01:04:20.330 --> 01:04:25.330
So, yesterday morning, in
order to get him to leave

01:04:25.410 --> 01:04:26.670
without the movie being over,

01:04:26.670 --> 01:04:28.800
I told him that I'd watch it with him.

01:04:28.800 --> 01:04:32.200
And it was The Pink Panther.

01:04:32.200 --> 01:04:33.033
- Original?

01:04:33.033 --> 01:04:34.950
- No, not the original,
that was with Peter Sellers.

01:04:34.950 --> 01:04:36.320
This was Pink Panther with--

01:04:36.320 --> 01:04:37.153
- Steve Martin?

01:04:37.153 --> 01:04:38.670
- Steve Martin which is the remake

01:04:40.286 --> 01:04:42.010
from the '90s.

01:04:42.010 --> 01:04:43.083
I'd never seen it.

01:04:44.370 --> 01:04:45.930
- It's since been remade again, right?

01:04:45.930 --> 01:04:48.530
- I don't know but he,

01:04:48.530 --> 01:04:50.740
he came up first thing in the morning,

01:04:50.740 --> 01:04:51.920
got in the bed with me and Christy

01:04:51.920 --> 01:04:54.660
and looks at me and he's like
you ready to watch the movie?

01:04:54.660 --> 01:04:56.160
And I'm like, oh yeah, I did promise that.

01:04:56.160 --> 01:04:57.290
So, like first thing--

01:04:57.290 --> 01:04:58.150
- Oh, to finish the movie?

01:04:58.150 --> 01:05:01.163
- Yesterday morning, no,
we started it over and,

01:05:02.290 --> 01:05:03.140
have you seen it?

01:05:04.640 --> 01:05:06.400
- I'm not sure.

01:05:06.400 --> 01:05:08.050
- It was really funny, man.

01:05:08.050 --> 01:05:11.240
I mean I've been deprived
of a lot of comedy

01:05:11.240 --> 01:05:12.490
and I realized that like,

01:05:13.446 --> 01:05:15.043
I didn't think I would find it funny

01:05:15.043 --> 01:05:18.680
because it's like a lot of
slapstick and it's very,

01:05:18.680 --> 01:05:21.930
but there's a whole layer of smart

01:05:21.930 --> 01:05:23.310
baked into how this thing was written.

01:05:23.310 --> 01:05:26.000
Now, it only got 21% on Rotten Tomatoes

01:05:26.000 --> 01:05:29.140
but you know what, I'm
taking back what I said

01:05:29.140 --> 01:05:32.230
when it comes to comedy,
probably horror too,

01:05:32.230 --> 01:05:33.960
it's not reliable.

01:05:33.960 --> 01:05:37.027
I think that at least the
first half of that movie

01:05:37.027 --> 01:05:39.730
is if you're in the right frame of mind

01:05:39.730 --> 01:05:42.540
and you take it for what
it is, it's very funny.

01:05:42.540 --> 01:05:45.170
It is very smart the way
that they have executed

01:05:45.170 --> 01:05:46.763
something that is so,

01:05:47.750 --> 01:05:51.010
well, not stupid but
oblivious, this character.

01:05:51.010 --> 01:05:52.930
Very funny, man, I highly recommend it.

01:05:52.930 --> 01:05:56.530
We had a blast, the two
of us just cackling.

01:05:56.530 --> 01:05:58.590
And it's all credit Shepherd for that.

01:05:58.590 --> 01:05:59.642
- Oh, he's a great

01:05:59.642 --> 01:06:00.793
movie critic.
- He loved that movie.

01:06:02.960 --> 01:06:06.270
2006, thanks, Jenna, so yeah, it came out.

01:06:06.270 --> 01:06:08.323
So yeah, not even in the '90s.

01:06:08.323 --> 01:06:09.460
That was a sequel

01:06:11.020 --> 01:06:13.300
that we haven't watched yet
but maybe we'll watch that.

01:06:13.300 --> 01:06:14.630
That's not our recommendations, though.

01:06:14.630 --> 01:06:15.890
Should we go to that?

01:06:15.890 --> 01:06:18.640
Let's put a capper on what we've
learned from our vacations.

01:06:18.640 --> 01:06:20.023
Fire and ice.

01:06:21.010 --> 01:06:23.630
Check your ego at the door.

01:06:23.630 --> 01:06:25.420
- Well, again, my mission,

01:06:25.420 --> 01:06:29.350
your mission was to relax,
my mission was to prepare

01:06:29.350 --> 01:06:33.983
for a longer trip and I was a
little bit worried about like,

01:06:33.983 --> 01:06:37.050
it's so cold, it was difficult conditions,

01:06:37.050 --> 01:06:38.950
great conditions but difficult conditions,

01:06:38.950 --> 01:06:41.130
is Shepard going to be,

01:06:41.130 --> 01:06:43.160
kids at that age, they
can go one of two ways.

01:06:43.160 --> 01:06:44.700
They can sort of recoil from it

01:06:44.700 --> 01:06:47.210
and sort of go into themselves
and then you're like oh, crap

01:06:47.210 --> 01:06:49.900
I've already paid for this
week long vacation in Colorado

01:06:49.900 --> 01:06:52.470
and now, I'm the only
one that wants to do it.

01:06:52.470 --> 01:06:54.500
When we left the mountain on the last day,

01:06:54.500 --> 01:06:57.400
Shepherd was like, do we have to leave?

01:06:57.400 --> 01:06:58.930
One more run, dad.

01:06:58.930 --> 01:07:00.510
And so he's on board.

01:07:00.510 --> 01:07:03.350
He was he was the one that
I was worried about, right?

01:07:03.350 --> 01:07:04.183
- That's good.

01:07:04.183 --> 01:07:06.730
I mean you did sweeten the
deal with the topless woman.

01:07:06.730 --> 01:07:07.580
- Right, now he just thinks

01:07:07.580 --> 01:07:09.350
that every time we go to the mountains,

01:07:09.350 --> 01:07:10.350
we ski during the day

01:07:10.350 --> 01:07:12.270
and then we watch naked ladies at night

01:07:12.270 --> 01:07:14.310
and I'm gonna have to,

01:07:14.310 --> 01:07:17.420
I'll have to correct that vision.

01:07:17.420 --> 01:07:18.560
- I feel like there are some things

01:07:18.560 --> 01:07:20.340
that have been discussed in this episode

01:07:20.340 --> 01:07:23.353
that we're gonna have to
apologize for but not.

01:07:25.440 --> 01:07:27.350
- And what did you learn?
- I didn't buy the banner.

01:07:27.350 --> 01:07:28.400
- You're not a bushy.

01:07:29.280 --> 01:07:31.190
- I might be, still don't know it means.

01:07:31.190 --> 01:07:34.260
- Maybe saying no to the
banner makes you a bushy.

01:07:34.260 --> 01:07:35.093
- Right.

01:07:36.270 --> 01:07:37.103
- Did you learn anything else?

01:07:37.103 --> 01:07:39.434
- No, I just learned
what happened with you.

01:07:39.434 --> 01:07:42.310
(laughing)

01:07:42.310 --> 01:07:43.608
Recs In Effect.

01:07:43.608 --> 01:07:45.941
♪ Check, baby, check, baby,
one, two, three, four ♪

01:07:45.941 --> 01:07:48.181
♪ Check, baby, check, baby, one, two ♪

01:07:48.181 --> 01:07:49.014
♪ Check, baby ♪

01:07:49.014 --> 01:07:49.847
♪ Check, baby, one ♪
- I've got a rec.

01:07:49.847 --> 01:07:53.080
I watched during the probably 20 of hours

01:07:53.080 --> 01:07:56.263
of flight that we took to and from London,

01:07:57.960 --> 01:08:01.543
I watched the entire Waco series.

01:08:02.600 --> 01:08:03.680
May have heard about this.

01:08:03.680 --> 01:08:05.440
- Waco, Texas.

01:08:05.440 --> 01:08:06.620
- So it's--
- Town.

01:08:06.620 --> 01:08:09.300
- It's on, I think it's on Paramount.

01:08:09.300 --> 01:08:12.770
Like the Paramount Network
which a lot of people don't have

01:08:12.770 --> 01:08:14.550
but they're trying some things.

01:08:14.550 --> 01:08:16.720
They're trying to establish themselves.

01:08:16.720 --> 01:08:19.313
- This is the Branch Davidians.

01:08:20.661 --> 01:08:23.570
Well, they don't call themselves a cult

01:08:23.570 --> 01:08:27.478
but well that's what the
US government call them.

01:08:27.478 --> 01:08:29.430
- They were definitely a cult.

01:08:29.430 --> 01:08:31.200
So, you remember David Koresh,

01:08:31.200 --> 01:08:34.890
the Branch Davidians,
early '90s, there was a,

01:08:34.890 --> 01:08:37.010
how many days would you
have said that the standoff

01:08:37.010 --> 01:08:38.610
between the Branch Davidians
and the government was?

01:08:38.610 --> 01:08:40.760
Because we were in high
school at the time.

01:08:41.950 --> 01:08:43.610
I remember hearing about it on the news

01:08:43.610 --> 01:08:44.443
but what's your guess how long?

01:08:44.443 --> 01:08:46.550
- They talked about it
a long time but I mean,

01:08:46.550 --> 01:08:48.030
I'm just gonna guess seven days.

01:08:48.030 --> 01:08:49.300
- 50 days.

01:08:49.300 --> 01:08:50.265
- 50 days?

01:08:50.265 --> 01:08:51.730
- Maybe 51 days.

01:08:51.730 --> 01:08:54.106
There was a standoff and it was,

01:08:54.106 --> 01:08:55.070
a really interesting,

01:08:55.070 --> 01:08:59.567
first of all, I think that back in the,

01:08:59.567 --> 01:09:02.290
let me just say that Taylor Kitsch,

01:09:02.290 --> 01:09:03.800
however you say his name,

01:09:03.800 --> 01:09:05.469
of Friday Night Lights fame.

01:09:05.469 --> 01:09:06.480
- [Link] Riggins.

01:09:06.480 --> 01:09:09.870
- Plays David Koresh and he's excellent.

01:09:09.870 --> 01:09:11.540
He's really, really good, very compelling

01:09:11.540 --> 01:09:14.440
and there's other like kind of a who's who

01:09:14.440 --> 01:09:18.010
of like sort of supporting
actors from other shows.

01:09:18.010 --> 01:09:20.560
- I'm glad he did good because he did bad.

01:09:20.560 --> 01:09:23.880
He was in that Disney movie
that cost a whole lot of money.

01:09:23.880 --> 01:09:25.260
- Oh, that was a little
bit of an embarrassment.

01:09:25.260 --> 01:09:26.690
- And yeah, that kinda--

01:09:26.690 --> 01:09:28.090
- But he was great in this.

01:09:28.090 --> 01:09:29.350
Showed a lot of versatility.

01:09:29.350 --> 01:09:31.730
It's very difficult to
be like taken seriously

01:09:31.730 --> 01:09:34.130
and like to be this like
compelling character

01:09:34.130 --> 01:09:36.973
with a mullet in that way and
he just kind of nailed it.

01:09:39.370 --> 01:09:44.370
But like the side piece
from House of Cards,

01:09:44.620 --> 01:09:46.010
like Claire Underwood side piece,

01:09:46.010 --> 01:09:48.893
that guy was in it and
then Supergirl was in it

01:09:48.893 --> 01:09:52.669
then the blonde curly
headed girl from Ozark.

01:09:52.669 --> 01:09:55.160
There's a lot of people you
go, oh, that guy from that,

01:09:55.160 --> 01:09:56.520
that girl from this.

01:09:56.520 --> 01:09:58.900
And I thought they did,

01:09:58.900 --> 01:10:01.730
I really enjoyed it 'cause
I like the historical aspect

01:10:01.730 --> 01:10:03.480
but the interesting thing about it

01:10:03.480 --> 01:10:06.520
is that there's the story that the FBI

01:10:06.520 --> 01:10:09.320
and the ATF kind of put
out about what happened

01:10:09.320 --> 01:10:12.750
which is the story that
as a kid in the '90s,

01:10:12.750 --> 01:10:16.290
listening to the news, you
get the government story

01:10:16.290 --> 01:10:18.050
and I'm not much of a conspiracy theorist

01:10:18.050 --> 01:10:20.260
as much as I like to say things
like Finland doesn't exist

01:10:20.260 --> 01:10:22.290
for funsies on GMM.

01:10:22.290 --> 01:10:25.300
I'm really not really prone
to believe conspiracies

01:10:25.300 --> 01:10:27.420
but it's interesting
because the whole series

01:10:27.420 --> 01:10:30.750
is from the perspective
of the FBI negotiator

01:10:30.750 --> 01:10:34.920
who basically got kicked off
of the job towards the end

01:10:34.920 --> 01:10:38.620
and a guy named David Thibodeau

01:10:38.620 --> 01:10:42.520
who was one of the cult
members who got out

01:10:42.520 --> 01:10:44.350
and kind of made it out
of this thing alive.

01:10:44.350 --> 01:10:46.900
And basically, it's like you heard

01:10:46.900 --> 01:10:49.210
that this was all the
stuff that was happening

01:10:49.210 --> 01:10:52.420
but this is our perspective
on what happened.

01:10:52.420 --> 01:10:55.740
So I'm sure that it's biased,
I'm sure that it's not true,

01:10:55.740 --> 01:10:58.417
100% true but you've got
sort of the government story

01:10:58.417 --> 01:11:00.990
and then you've got the
Branch Davidians story

01:11:00.990 --> 01:11:03.280
and it's just very interesting
to see that perspective

01:11:03.280 --> 01:11:04.340
like oh, this kind of makes me,

01:11:04.340 --> 01:11:08.450
I wonder what actually went
down, but I recommend it.

01:11:08.450 --> 01:11:10.783
It's only six episodes so
it's one of those things

01:11:10.783 --> 01:11:12.650
that there's not too much of a commitment

01:11:12.650 --> 01:11:16.480
to just see the story played
out and it's well executed.

01:11:16.480 --> 01:11:18.290
- So, are you a Branch Davidian now?

01:11:18.290 --> 01:11:20.180
- No, I'm definitely
not a Branch Davidian.

01:11:20.180 --> 01:11:21.690
David Koresh was very wack

01:11:21.690 --> 01:11:25.480
and did a bunch of
really ridiculous things

01:11:25.480 --> 01:11:27.700
but I don't necessarily think

01:11:27.700 --> 01:11:29.990
that they should have been

01:11:31.870 --> 01:11:34.060
executed by the government.

01:11:34.060 --> 01:11:36.137
- That's the rec for this week.

